@page
@model StaffModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Information for Staff";
}

<section class="page-banner">
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Kasper College Staff Portal &amp; Faculty Information</h1>
        <p>Official Guidance, Academic Administration, IT Services, HR Policies, and Campus Facilities for Staff.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="staff-news">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 id="staff-news">1. News &amp; College Announcements</h2>
        <div class="grid-cards">
            <article class="card">
                <h3>Software Engineering Student of the Year Awards</h3>
                <p>Kasper College recently hosted the annual National Software Engineering Student of the Year Awards in the Main Lecture Theatre. Shortlisted candidates from 24 institutions nationwide attended the one-day symposium and showcase.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>&pound;1.2M High-Performance Computing Grant</h3>
                <p>The Department of Computing &amp; Digital Technologies has been awarded &pound;1.2 million from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council (EPSRC) to install a cutting-edge GPU cluster dedicated to AI ethics and edge-computing research.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <h3>National Teaching Fellowships</h3>
                <p>Congratulations to Dr. Sarah Jenkins (Senior Lecturer in Cyber Security) and Prof. David Chen (Reader in Interactive Media) on being awarded National Teaching Fellowships for pedagogical innovation.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-block section-alt" aria-labelledby="staff-admin">
    <div class="container two-col">
        <article class="card">
            <h2 id="staff-admin">2. Academic Registry &amp; Quality Assurance</h2>
            <p>The Academic Registry oversees academic regulations, assessment standards, student records, module evaluation, and course validation.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Assessment &amp; Moderation:</strong> All summative assessment briefs must undergo internal peer moderation 4 weeks prior to release. Sample scripts (10% or minimum 6 scripts) must be submitted for external examiner scrutiny.</li>
                <li><strong>Grade Submission Deadlines:</strong> Autumn semester module results must be finalized on the Student Records System (SRS) by 17:00 on Friday, 22 January 2027.</li>
                <li><strong>Extenuating Circumstances &amp; Academic Appeals:</strong> Faculty panels review claims weekly. Staff should direct distressed students to the Student Support Desk for initial evidence validation.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <h2>3. Human Resources, Payroll &amp; Staff Wellbeing</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>HR Service Portal:</strong> Staff can access monthly payslips, P60s, annual leave booking (35 days plus bank holidays), and sickness reporting via the internal PeopleHR portal.</li>
                <li><strong>Employee Assistance Programme (EAP):</strong> Free 24/7 confidential counseling, financial advice, and mental health support available to all permanent and fixed-term staff via HealthAssured (Freephone: 0800 030 5182).</li>
                <li><strong>Staff Development Fund:</strong> Full-time faculty are eligible for up to &pound;1,500 annually toward conference attendance, professional certifications (e.g., AWS, Cisco, Adobe), and academic journal publication fees.</li>
                <li><strong>Cycle-to-Work &amp; EV Salary Sacrifice:</strong> Tax-free bicycle purchases and electric vehicle leasing schemes available through the HR Benefits hub.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <h2>4. IT Services &amp; Classroom Technology Support</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Single Sign-On (SSO) &amp; MFA:</strong> All staff accounts require Microsoft Authenticator multi-factor authentication for logging into campus systems and remote VPN access.</li>
                <li><strong>Moodle VLE &amp; Panopto Lecture Capture:</strong> All lecture theatres and seminar rooms feature automated recording. Course materials and reading lists must be populated 2 weeks before teaching commences.</li>
                <li><strong>Classroom AV Hotline:</strong> Immediate in-class technical assistance is available by dialing extension 2222 from any lectern telephone.</li>
                <li><strong>Software Licenses:</strong> Staff may request specialized software installations for teaching labs by submitting an IT Helpdesk ticket at least 15 working days prior to term start.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <h2>5. Room Bookings, 6. Health &amp; Safety, 7. Catering</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Timetabled Teaching Rooms:</strong> Managed centrally by the Academic Timetabling Team. Ad-hoc bookings for extra tutorials or student workshops can be made via the Resource Scheduler system.</li>
                <li><strong>Specialist Computing Labs:</strong> SOC labs, VR suites, and maker workshops require certified technician supervision when booked outside standard timetable hours.</li>
                <li><strong>Conference &amp; Meeting Rooms:</strong> The Boardroom (Room 302) and Executive Suite (Room 305) can be reserved via Outlook calendar invites.</li>
                <li><strong>Emergency Numbers:</strong> Campus Security &amp; First Aid Emergency: dial 3333 (Internal) or (01321) 2340 333.</li>
                <li><strong>Fire Alarm Testing:</strong> Conducted every Tuesday at 08:45. Evacuate immediately via the nearest fire exit to Assembly Point A (Main Campus Plaza) or Point B (West Car Park).</li>
                <li><strong>Display Screen Equipment (DSE):</strong> All staff must complete an annual DSE self-assessment to ensure ergonomic workstation setup.</li>
                <li><strong>Catering &amp; Hospitality Bookings:</strong> Contact Catering Services (<a href="mailto:catering@kaspercollege.ac.uk">catering@kaspercollege.ac.uk</a>) at least 48 hours in advance.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

